{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019jYPmQbLP8fEmE8gRi6o9b","type":"tool_result","content":"320\t- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n321\t  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n322\t  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n323\t  exit 2 with a named error.\n324\t- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n325\t  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n326\t  which reads as green.\n327\t- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n328\t  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n329\t- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n330\t  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n331\t  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n332\t- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n333\t  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n334\t- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n335\t  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n336\t  directory.\n337\t\n338\t### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n339\t\n340\t- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n341\t  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n342\t- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n343\t  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n344\t  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n345\t  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n346\t  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n347\t\n348\t### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n349\t\n350\t- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n351\t  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n352\t  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n353\t- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n354\t  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n355\t  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n356\t- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n357\t  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n358\t- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n359\t  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`\n360\t    on Python 3.13 and later, so a baseline recorded on 3.9 to 3.12 no\n361\t    longer reads as phantom sites on 3.13 and 3.14. The push run of\n362\t    `validate.yml` has no 3.14 leg; the scheduled run on that commit\n363\t    passed on 2026-11-03, its Python 3.14 leg included.\n364\t  - The ownership e2e check C.3 finds the canonical guards through the"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e98cc69-9185-4f95-b319-4d1b22b49864","uuid":"ee894c9e-a265-4176-b842-729e7ab255d9","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:14:10.445Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n  exit 2 with a named error.\n- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n  which reads as green.\n- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It\n  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n  directory.\n\n### Changed — `/ceo-boot` and other files that reach installs\n\n- `/ceo-boot` adds `main_checkout_state`. It is yellow, never red, when the\n  main checkout is off its default branch or on a detached HEAD.\n- The installer copies every top-level `.claude/scripts/*.py`, so six new\n  maintenance helpers reach installs: `_contamination_inventory.py`,\n  `_repin_guard.py`, `_restore_archive.py`, `_subprocess_census.py`,\n  `caller_repo_guard.py` and `check-subprocess-tests.py`. `ceo-restore.sh`\n  uses `_restore_archive.py`.\n\n### Changed — the framework's own CI and release (no installed file changes)\n\n- `scripts/install-npm.sh`, the local packaging check, reads the\n  `npm pack --json` output of npm 12.2 and later, which keys the record by\n  package name. Publishing still pins npm 11.20.0.\n- CI runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The repository variable\n  `VM_CI_ENABLED` is unset, so the self-hosted route that `[1.4.3]`\n  describes is off (measured 2026-11-03).\n- Release automation for the maintainer's Mac: `make mac-sign-merge`,\n  `make mac-cut-rc` and `make mac-cut-ga`.\n- Two red nightly runs on the merge of pull request #7 are cured:\n  - The subprocess census fingerprint pins `ast.dump(..., show_empty=True)`\n    on Python 3.13 and later, so a baseline recorded on 3.9 to 3.12 no\n    longer reads as phantom sites on 3.13 and 3.14. The push run of\n    `validate.yml` has no 3.14 leg; the scheduled run on that commit\n    passed on 2026-11-03, its Python 3.14 leg included.\n  - The ownership e2e check C.3 finds the canonical guards through the","numLines":45,"startLine":320,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019jYPmQbLP8fEmE8gRi6o9b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
