{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NywoGz9qXoNTptKo8FJoxd","type":"tool_result","content":"975\t  - **The rest stays open, and no release is assigned to their cure.**\n976\t  - The `defaultMode` change above is not the cure of any annex condition.\n977\t  - The list is in the sources the `[1.4.2]` entry names.\n978\t- **The v1.4.2 rc.1 annex, which the `[1.4.2]` entry does not name.** The\n979\t  three P1 findings of the signed rc.1 annex stayed open at the v1.4.2 GA\n980\t  (its condition 13), with no release promised for their cure, and this\n981\t  release does not cure them. By shape:\n982\t  - An inspection CLI that receives another checkout's path imports a\n983\t    Python module from that checkout's tree, so that module's import-time\n984\t    code runs with the caller's privileges.\n985\t  - A command a CLI prints for the operator to paste carries an unquoted\n986\t    path, so a directory name that contains a command substitution runs it\n987\t    when the command is pasted.\n988\t  - The re-pin pack generator does not normalize tarball member names the\n989\t    way the npm extractor does. Two members can then land on the same\n990\t    destination, and the pack can pin the bytes of a member the extractor\n991\t    does not leave there.\n992\t  - The P2 findings of that annex (condition 14) stay open too. One is a\n993\t    re-pin generator that writes `TODO(owner)` into prose that its own\n994\t    guard then refuses.\n995\t- **The Known-open of the `[1.4.2]` entry stays open as written there**,\n996\t  with two notes:\n997\t  - The Codex hook-host range now admits 0.160.x (above).\n998\t  - The CI test jobs now fetch the full history with tags. So the test that\n999\t    runs `derive-settings-baselines.py --check` runs there instead of being\n1000\t    skipped.\n1001\t- **What v1.4.1 left open stays open.** The `[1.4.2]` entry lists its\n1002\t  sources. This release does not change the Workflow guard and ledger, the\n1003\t  PLAN-190 recovery tools, or `upgrade.sh`.\n1004\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e98cc69-9185-4f95-b319-4d1b22b49864","uuid":"3b6e88a4-a453-4f3b-b8c2-0174a33d81c1","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:14:20.086Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  - **The rest stays open, and no release is assigned to their cure.**\n  - The `defaultMode` change above is not the cure of any annex condition.\n  - The list is in the sources the `[1.4.2]` entry names.\n- **The v1.4.2 rc.1 annex, which the `[1.4.2]` entry does not name.** The\n  three P1 findings of the signed rc.1 annex stayed open at the v1.4.2 GA\n  (its condition 13), with no release promised for their cure, and this\n  release does not cure them. By shape:\n  - An inspection CLI that receives another checkout's path imports a\n    Python module from that checkout's tree, so that module's import-time\n    code runs with the caller's privileges.\n  - A command a CLI prints for the operator to paste carries an unquoted\n    path, so a directory name that contains a command substitution runs it\n    when the command is pasted.\n  - The re-pin pack generator does not normalize tarball member names the\n    way the npm extractor does. Two members can then land on the same\n    destination, and the pack can pin the bytes of a member the extractor\n    does not leave there.\n  - The P2 findings of that annex (condition 14) stay open too. One is a\n    re-pin generator that writes `TODO(owner)` into prose that its own\n    guard then refuses.\n- **The Known-open of the `[1.4.2]` entry stays open as written there**,\n  with two notes:\n  - The Codex hook-host range now admits 0.160.x (above).\n  - The CI test jobs now fetch the full history with tags. So the test that\n    runs `derive-settings-baselines.py --check` runs there instead of being\n    skipped.\n- **What v1.4.1 left open stays open.** The `[1.4.2]` entry lists its\n  sources. This release does not change the Workflow guard and ledger, the\n  PLAN-190 recovery tools, or `upgrade.sh`.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":975,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NywoGz9qXoNTptKo8FJoxd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
