{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBtcWUmX3BZM4AZ4sL421B","type":"tool_result","content":"37:- Several of the largest hooks and scripts become thin entry points over\n38:  modules under `.claude/hooks/_lib/` (PLAN-197, ADR-202). A hook you\n39-  patched by hand must be patched again in its module.\n40-- A registered hook no longer drains the audit spool at exit (a partial\n41-  cure).\n42-- The model checks accept model families, among them other vendors' ids\n43-  and retired ids, and the Codex pin check accepts a newer Codex CLI on a\n44-  version floor, without a matching hash (Security and governance, below).\n--\n110:### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n111-\n112:- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n113-  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n114-  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n115-  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n116-  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n117-  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n118-- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n--\n212:- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n213-  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n214-  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and\n215-  audit emit). The same train replaced the plan-path regexes of two\n216-  kernel files, the plan-lifecycle hook (`check_plan_edit.py`) and the\n217-  policy preprocessors (`_lib/policy_preprocessors.py`), with the\n218-  plan-path predicate in `_lib/plan_paths.py`. The kernel's hard-deny\n--\n330:  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n331-  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n332-- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n333-  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n334-- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n335-  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n336-  directory."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e98cc69-9185-4f95-b319-4d1b22b49864","uuid":"d9582616-db8b-4f79-bdfb-71a28c124fdd","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:17:29.447Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"37:- Several of the largest hooks and scripts become thin entry points over\n38:  modules under `.claude/hooks/_lib/` (PLAN-197, ADR-202). A hook you\n39-  patched by hand must be patched again in its module.\n40-- A registered hook no longer drains the audit spool at exit (a partial\n41-  cure).\n42-- The model checks accept model families, among them other vendors' ids\n43-  and retired ids, and the Codex pin check accepts a newer Codex CLI on a\n44-  version floor, without a matching hash (Security and governance, below).\n--\n110:### Changed — hooks and scripts split into modules (PLAN-197, ADR-202)\n111-\n112:- Entry points keep their paths and their observable contracts. Their\n113-  implementations move into packages under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. For\n114-  example, `_lib/audit_emit.py` goes from 14,522 lines to 496, and\n115-  `check_bash_safety.py` becomes a 42-line entry point. Among the scripts,\n116-  `audit-query.py`, `check_contamination.py` and\n117-  `check-installer-write-safety.py` move the same way.\n118-- Installs and upgrades receive the packages: the installer copies every\n--\n212:- The split (PLAN-197) moved the code of seven kernel entry points into\n213-  helper packages: five hooks (canonical edit, pair rail, agent spawn,\n214-  audit log and Bash safety) and two hook library modules (policy and\n215-  audit emit). The same train replaced the plan-path regexes of two\n216-  kernel files, the plan-lifecycle hook (`check_plan_edit.py`) and the\n217-  policy preprocessors (`_lib/policy_preprocessors.py`), with the\n218-  plan-path predicate in `_lib/plan_paths.py`. The kernel's hard-deny\n--\n330:  reports `root_load_unobservable` unless you pass a complete list of the\n331-  loaded instruction files with `--instruction-load-evidence`.\n332-- The plan-lifecycle hook recognizes `PLAN-NNN-FOLLOWUP-<slug>.md` names\n333-  (`_lib/plan_paths.py`).\n334-- `check_cost_envelope.py` evaluates nothing, and records no spend, without\n335-  an absolute `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`. Before, it fell back to the current\n336-  directory.","numLines":34,"totalLines":34},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GBtcWUmX3BZM4AZ4sL421B","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
