ection.\n  - Writes stay where they were: the profiler writes to its tempdirs, the ledger to .claude/scripts/local/calibration-history.csv under repo_root, and the generator to the pack directory.\n  - Standard library only. I found no syntax or API newer than Python 3.9.\n- Declared conditions this payload touches\n  - Condition 7 is TRUE: the paths are kept and the logic moved to _lib modules.\n  - Conditions 9 and 10: the generator is consistent with the open-floor pin the CHANGELOG describes (CHANGELOG:199-201).\n  - Condition 2 is TRUE. The new generation-time TODO(owner) check partly addresses a P2 in the v1.4.2-rc.1 annex: before, the generator could write TODO(owner) into prose that its own guard then refuses. CHANGELOG [1.4.4]:435-436 does not claim that cure, and condition 2 explicitly does not say nothing changed in the range.\n  - Nothing in this payload makes a declared condition FALSE. I found no P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1. The one P1-class defect visible in this payload is already a signed lane note (codex-p11, claude-p11), so I am not adding it again: the profiler's isolation leaves CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH in the environment it passes to the hooks it measures (latency.py:119-127). diagnose-output-hook.py:29-33 strips the full list.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1. .claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py:496-497 with :2171 (carried from the rc1 lane notes, still open)\n- Scenario: the live pin is the open floor >=0.128.0, so upper is None. plan_range returns a bounded range with widened=True, and old_upper is set equal to new_upper.\n- Four rendered texts then state a widening that never happened (\"<A -> <A\"):\n  - the pin .new paragraph (:1676);\n  - the commit message (:1438);\n  - the sentinel Scope line the Owner signs (:1744);\n  - the README (:1611).\n- In the constants mold, OLD_UPPER only feeds printf lines (PLAN-194 OWNER-PIN-SIGN.sh:106, :448, :562). The effect is misleading signed text, not a wrong pin.\n- Fix: carry a distinct state, for example 