y points keep ... their observable contracts\\\".\\n- The only workflow that runs it, reality-ledger.yml:54-75, is advisory and exits 0 whatever happens.\\n- Fix: move the import and the install() call inside that try.\\n\\nP2-3. .claude/scripts/_repin_guard.py:6-7 against re-pin-codex.py:199, :203-204\\n- TODO_MARK, PIN_OUT and the generator path written into GUARD[0] are now defined in two files. _LEGACY_GUARD and the _GUARD[0] match (:1344) only agree because those values happen to be the same.\\n- Fix: import TODO_MARK and PIN_OUT from _repin_guard in re-pin-codex.py, or have a test assert they are equal.\\n\\nP2-4. CHANGELOG.md [1.4.4] (honesty by omission, not a false promise)\\n- The entry names _repin_guard.py only as a maintenance helper the installer now copies (:342-346). It does not mention any of the generator's changes:\\n  - the guard now reads literal paths;\\n  - a grep failure is now a refusal;\\n  - the generation-time TODO(owner) refusal;\\n  - the open-floor parsing that bounds the range when a pack is generated.\\n- Fix: add one line under the maintainer changes.\\n\\nP2-5. Housekeeping\\n- .claude/governance/function-length-grandfather.yaml:1454-1465 still lists profile-opus-4-7.py smoke_checks and main. Both now live in _profile_opus_parts/smoke.py and cli.py. The lint is advisory under ADR-097.\\n- .github/CODEOWNERS:122 names only the profiler's entry point, not _profile_opus_parts/ or _reality_ledger_parts/.\",\"decision\":\"GO\",\"sentence\":\"Against the candidate tree, payload 33 moves the profiler and reality-ledger logic into modules that keep its name lookup, patch points, fail direction and installation, and hardens the re-pin generator's guard; no declared condition is false, there is no P0 and no new P1, and what remains is P2 follow-ups.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"PAYLOAD 33/34: .claude/scripts/profile-opus-4-7.py, .claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py, .claude/scripts/reality-ledger.py\n\nSCOPE AND METHOD\nI read the three candidate entry points and the code they now load:\n- .claude/hooks/_lib/_profile_opus_parts/ (__init__, smoke, reference, latency, cli, hook_latency_docs)\n- .claude/hooks/_lib/_reality_ledger_parts/ (all ten modules)\n- .claude/scripts/_repin_guard.py\nI compared the moved bodies with the text this diff removes. I also checked:\n- the callers: validate.yml, reality-ledger.yml, diagnose-output-hook.py:79-83, check-substrate-drift.py:414-430;\n- the install path: scripts/install.sh:1524-1541 copies each top-level _lib entry, and :1606-1611 copies every .claude/scripts/*.py, which includes _repin_guard.py, as CHANGELOG:342-346 says;\n- the PLAN-194 constants mold, to see what it does with the values the generator writes.\nThis was a static review only. I executed no code.\n\nWHAT HOLDS\n- profile-opus-4-7.py\n  - install() rebuilds every function with FunctionType over the entry point's own globals. Values are deep-copied, so a patch on the entry point reaches the logic and the template modules stay untouched.\n  - Every name the four modules use is imported by the entry point (:49-61) or defined in a sibling module. No name is defined in two modules.\n  - _REF_EXEC_SOURCE is byte-identical, so ref_source_sha256 is stable.\n  - The 103-line docstring of run_hook_latency is put back by install() (__init__.py:61-62).\n  - Adding .claude/hooks to sys.path shadows no standard-library module: no hooks/*.py has a stdlib name, and there is no .claude/scripts/_lib.\n- reality-ledger.py\n  - The ten modules export through __all__. Shared constants come in once, through constants.py.\n  - The classes are rebuilt with methods rebound, staticmethods included.\n  - _REPO_ROOT, redact_secrets and the itimer helpers still come from the entry point (:52-69).\n  - The self-exclusion gains \"/_reality_ledger_parts/\" (constants.py:55). The detector's findings on its own CEO_* reads therefore stay as they were when reality-ledger.py was excluded by basename.\n  - The fallback added to _read_known_actions (audit_actions.py:38-114) parses files and never imports them. It never runs today: audit_emit.py:45 still holds the literal _KNOWN_ACTIONS, and \"actions\" is not in the install list (audit_emit.py:415-451). The detector reads the set that is live at runtime.\n- re-pin-codex.py\n  - _GUARD[0] in _repin_guard.py equals _LEGACY_GUARD[0], so older packs are still recognised as molds (:1344-1349).\n  - The new guard reads paths the generator writes as literals, restricted to [A-Za-z0-9._/-] (:939-963), so no shell metacharacters can enter. It runs grep with env -u GREP_OPTIONS LC_ALL=C grep -F, and a grep exit code of 2 or more now refuses instead of passing. That is the intended fail-closed direction for this maintainer ceremony.\n  - _check_guard_read_files (:966-977) is consistent with the pending fields the generator writes (:1694, :1761, :1822). The inherited-prose note no longer contains TODO(owner) (:1598).\n  - parse_pin accepts the live open floor \">=0.128.0\" (.claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:199). Without that change the generator would refuse the live pin with EXIT_INPUT.\n- check-substrate-drift.py loads re-pin-codex.py through spec_from_file_location (:414-430).\n  - Any exception is caught and reported (fail-open, named).\n  - It sets dont_write_bytecode first (:1261).\n  - Run as a script, .claude/scripts is sys.path[0], so the _repin_guard import resolves.\n- General\n  - None of the three files is a registered hook. Nothing here disables a governance hook, changes a model or effort, or blocks a session. I found no inversion of fail direction.\n  - Writes stay where they were: the profiler writes to its tempdirs, the ledger to .claude/scripts/local/calibration-history.csv under repo_root, and the generator to the pack directory.\n  - Standard library only. I found no syntax or API newer than Python 3.9.\n- Declared conditions this payload touches\n  - Condition 7 is TRUE: the paths are kept and the logic moved to _lib modules.\n  - Conditions 9 and 10: the generator is consistent with the open-floor pin the CHANGELOG describes (CHANGELOG:199-201).\n  - Condition 2 is TRUE. The new generation-time TODO(owner) check partly addresses a P2 in the v1.4.2-rc.1 annex: before, the generator could write TODO(owner) into prose that its own guard then refuses. CHANGELOG [1.4.4]:435-436 does not claim that cure, and condition 2 explicitly does not say nothing changed in the range.\n  - Nothing in this payload makes a declared condition FALSE. I found no P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1. The one P1-class defect visible in this payload is already a signed lane note (codex-p11, claude-p11), so I am not adding it again: the profiler's isolation leaves CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH in the environment it passes to the hooks it measures (latency.py:119-127). diagnose-output-hook.py:29-33 strips the full list.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1. .claude/scripts/re-pin-codex.py:496-497 with :2171 (carried from the rc1 lane notes, still open)\n- Scenario: the live pin is the open floor >=0.128.0, so upper is None. plan_range returns a bounded range with widened=True, and old_upper is set equal to new_upper.\n- Four rendered texts then state a widening that never happened (\"<A -> <A\"):\n  - the pin .new paragraph (:1676);\n  - the commit message (:1438);\n  - the sentinel Scope line the Owner signs (:1744);\n  - the README (:1611).\n- In the constants mold, OLD_UPPER only feeds printf lines (PLAN-194 OWNER-PIN-SIGN.sh:106, :448, :562). The effect is misleading signed text, not a wrong pin.\n- Fix: carry a distinct state, for example widened=\"bounded-from-floor\", and render \"open floor >=L -> bounded >=L,<N\" in all four places.\n\nP2-2. .claude/scripts/reality-ledger.py:81-83 (carried from the rc1 lane notes)\n- Scenario: the import of the new modules sits outside the FATAL ImportError block (:58-69). A partial install exits 1 with a traceback instead of the documented \"2 = detector internal error\". That goes against CHANGELOG:112, \"Entry points keep ... their observable contracts\".\n- The only workflow that runs it, reality-ledger.yml:54-75, is advisory and exits 0 whatever happens.\n- Fix: move the import and the install() call inside that try.\n\nP2-3. .claude/scripts/_repin_guard.py:6-7 against re-pin-codex.py:199, :203-204\n- TODO_MARK, PIN_OUT and the generator path written into GUARD[0] are now defined in two files. _LEGACY_GUARD and the _GUARD[0] match (:1344) only agree because those values happen to be the same.\n- Fix: import TODO_MARK and PIN_OUT from _repin_guard in re-pin-codex.py, or have a test assert they are equal.\n\nP2-4. CHANGELOG.md [1.4.4] (honesty by omission, not a false promise)\n- The entry names _repin_guard.py only as a maintenance helper the installer now copies (:342-346). It does not mention any of the generator's changes:\n  - the guard now reads literal paths;\n  - a grep failure is now a refusal;\n  - the generation-time TODO(owner) refusal;\n  - the open-floor parsing that bounds the range when a pack is generated.\n- Fix: add one line under the maintainer changes.\n\nP2-5. Housekeeping\n- .claude/governance/function-length-grandfather.yaml:1454-1465 still lists profile-opus-4-7.py smoke_checks and main. Both now live in _profile_opus_parts/smoke.py and cli.py. The lint is advisory under ADR-097.\n- .github/CODEOWNERS:122 names only the profiler's entry point, not _profile_opus_parts/ or _reality_ledger_parts/.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Against the candidate tree, payload 33 moves the profiler and reality-ledger logic into modules that keep its name lookup, patch points, fail direction and installation, and hardens the re-pin generator's guard; no declared condition is false, there is no P0 and no new P1, and what remains is P2 follow-ups."},"ttft_ms":7060,"type":"result","duration_ms":502977,"uuid":"ba478187-5d1c-43eb-8d60-42d8beaa5d0d","ttft_stream_ms":5468,"time_to_request_ms":221,"first_content_frame_ms":5468,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_